# Poducator — secrets required by the server function (api/session.js).
#
# This file documents WHICH secrets are needed. It never contains values, and
# no file in this repo ever should: the repository is public, so anything
# committed here is published, and git history keeps it published even after a
# later removal.
#
# Set these in the Vercel dashboard: Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

# Your Anthropic API key. Lives only in the function's environment — it is
# never sent to a browser and never appears in the client bundle. The function
# has no passphrase gate, so set a spend limit on this key in the Anthropic
# console — that is what bounds cost if the URL gets passed around.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL — premium voices (docs/premium-audio.md). When set, live lessons are
# spoken by OpenAI's text-to-speech instead of the browser's built-in voices;
# when unset, the app quietly keeps the browser voices. Same rules as above:
# set it as a Vercel environment variable only, and set a usage limit on the key in the
# OpenAI dashboard.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL — override the speech model (default: gpt-4o-mini-tts).
# OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=
